    "title": "Coach Zo, an Oakland football legend, hits the national spotlight - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Nick Lozito ,\n1 days ago To Alonzo Carter, the message from the Oakland hilltop was clear: You can’t touch this. That went for all of Coach John Beam’s rivals looking to wrestle Oakland Athletic League football supremacy from Skyline High throughout most of the 1990s. McClymonds was a basketball school in those days with dwindling enrollment, but then Carter, a West Oakland kid who’d made good as a dancer with MC Hammer, got the school’s top coaching job and put the public-school league on notice with a gusto that might have made Hammer himself blush. Carter cultivated a look with his orange-and-black fatigues and combat boots. He rode his motorcycle right onto the field. And he talked trash with rival coaches, especially his friend Delton Edwards, the coach at Oakland Tech. Read full article\n5",
    "summary": "5 hours ago To Alonzo Carter, the message from the Oakland hilltop was clear: You can’t touch this. That went for all of Coach John Beam’s rivals looking to wrestle Oakland Athletic League football supremacy from Skyline High throughout most of the 1990s. McClymonds was a basketball school in those days with dwindling enrollment, but then Carter, a West Oakland kid who’d made good as a dancer with MC Hammer, got the school’s top coaching job and put the public-school league on notice with a gusto that might have made Hammer himself blush.",
